---@class posthog.integrations.PushTokenImportFailure
---@field index number Position of the row in the request's `subscriptions`, from 0.
---@field distinct_id string The distinct ID of the row.
---@field device_token_suffix string The last 6 characters of the row's device token, to find the row.
---@field reason posthog.integrations.PushTokenImportFailureReasonEnum Why the device was not stored. `unknown_person`: no person has this distinct ID, so check the ID or set `create_missing_persons`. `token_mismatch`: the token is the wrong kind for this channel, for example an Expo token, or an APNs token on a Firebase channel. `not_stored` and `person_processing_disabled`: ingestion did not store the device. * `unknown_person` - No person has this distinct ID * `token_mismatch` - The token does not fit this channel * `not_stored` - The device was not stored * `person_processing_disabled` - Person processing is off for this person
---@field detail string A sentence a person can act on.

---* `unknown_person` - No person has this distinct ID
---* `token_mismatch` - The token does not fit this channel
---* `not_stored` - The device was not stored
---* `person_processing_disabled` - Person processing is off for this person
---@alias posthog.integrations.PushTokenImportFailureReasonEnum "unknown_person"|"token_mismatch"|"not_stored"|"person_processing_disabled"

